    {
      "id": "O02",
      "verdict": "confirmed",
      "reason": "The first Do holds the mutex while its function runs and sets done before unlocking. A concurrent Do that sees done as false must acquire the mutex and recheck done, then skip its own function. TestOnceConcurrentWait checks for early return during a 50 ms window, completion after release, and whether the second function ran. The timeout shows only bounded nonreturn and can pass even if the second goroutine was never scheduled before release. The source establishes the wait guarantee.",
      "line": 74,
      "fragment": "o.m.Lock()"
    }
  ]
